# Living strawberry cursor

Status: DONE PUBLIC
Milestone: M75 Reactive, continuously changing cursor silhouette
Dependencies: 79_WIDE_THEMED_GLASS_AND_LIVENESS.todo (shared final release)

## Purpose

The owner wants the strawberry follower to feel alive rather than remain a
perfect circle. Use bounded organic deformation and direction-responsive oval
stretching, retaining its pale colour, current trail and native-pointer safeguards.
The same release must finish79's smallest-phone glass visibility correction.

## Tasks

- [x] Preserve the published controller, material, model, CSS and tests.
- [x] Add smooth idle morphing and velocity-directed stretch to the cursor only.
- [x] Keep shape, material shading and strawberry tint aligned; prevent crop clipping.
- [x] Prove ambient output/model/time, trail, click targets and fallbacks unchanged locally.
- [x] Strengthen small-phone visibility through green glass without losing contrast locally.
- [x] Publish the reviewed changes and repeat live motion/glass/cursor checks.
- [x] Close79 and80 only after the actual live checks pass.

## Acceptance criteria

- The resting follower changes shape; moving it produces a smooth reactive oval.
- Shapes are soft and bounded, not flickering, jagged or enlarged without limit.
- Strawberry colour and trail remain; no input interception or extra controls.
- Ambient2Xmovement and full-column themed glass remain intact.
- Pause, native viewers, reduced motion and graphics failure retain normal pointers.
- Existing148photos, original sources and local4174study are preserved; matching artwork is refreshed only for the glass change.

